Permanently moving data from one storage location, system, or format to another. This process often follows best practices set by federal agencies like NIST (National Institute of Standards and Technology). Some key aspects of data migration involve keeping the data secure, ensuring data accuracy, minimizing downtime, creating clear documentation, and testing to ensure everything works after the migration.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:1:{s:24:"glossary:cloud_migration";b:0;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:4:{s:4:"date";a:1:{s:7:"created";i:1744830240;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744830240;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"C";s:2:"id";s:23:"glossary:data_migration";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:7:"created";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:808;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}}}